## Setup

Place $B=(0,0)$, $C=(15,0)$. From $AB=13$, $AC=14$:
$$x_A^2+y_A^2=169,\quad (x_A-15)^2+y_A^2=196 \implies x_A=\tfrac{33}{5},\; y_A=\tfrac{56}{5}.$$
So $A=(\tfrac{33}{5},\tfrac{56}{5})$.

**Key points:**
- $D = (\tfrac{33}{5},0)$ (foot from $A$ to $BC$).
- Orthocenter $H$: altitude from $B$ is perpendicular to $AC$ (slope $-\tfrac43$), so it has slope $\tfrac34$: $y=\tfrac34 x$. At $x=\tfrac{33}{5}$: $H=(\tfrac{33}{5},\tfrac{99}{20})$.
- $E$ on $BC$ via angle-bisector theorem: $BE:EC=13:14$, so $E=(\tfrac{65}{9},0)$.

## Feet $P$, $Q$ and line $PQ$

Projecting $E$ onto $AB$ and $AC$:
$$P=\Big(\tfrac{121}{65},\tfrac{616}{195}\Big),\qquad Q=\Big(\tfrac{61}{5},\tfrac{56}{15}\Big).$$
Direction $\overrightarrow{PQ} \propto (2016,112)\propto (18,1)$, so $PQ$ has direction $(18,1)$.

## Point $K$ (foot from $D$ to $PQ$)

Parametrize $PQ: P + u(18,1)$. With $D-P = (\tfrac{924}{195},-\tfrac{616}{195})$:
$$u=\frac{(D-P)\cdot(18,1)}{18^2+1^2}=\frac{16016/195}{325}=\frac{1232}{4875},$$
$$K=P+u(18,1)=\Big(\tfrac{10417}{1625},\tfrac{5544}{1625}\Big).$$

## Computing $\tan\angle HBK$

$$\overrightarrow{BH}=\Big(\tfrac{33}{5},\tfrac{99}{20}\Big),\quad \overrightarrow{BK}=\Big(\tfrac{10417}{1625},\tfrac{5544}{1625}\Big).$$

Cross and dot (common denominator $20\cdot1625=32500$):
$$\overrightarrow{BH}\times\overrightarrow{BK}=\frac{33\cdot5544\cdot4-99\cdot10417}{32500}=\frac{731808-1031283}{32500}=\frac{-299475}{32500},$$
$$\overrightarrow{BH}\cdot\overrightarrow{BK}=\frac{33\cdot10417\cdot4+99\cdot5544}{32500}=\frac{1375044+548856}{32500}=\frac{1923900}{32500}.$$
$$\tan\angle HBK=\frac{299475}{1923900}=\frac{33}{212}.$$

## Verifying $\tan\angle HCK = \tfrac{33}{212}$

$$\overrightarrow{CH}=\Big(\tfrac{-42}{5},\tfrac{99}{20}\Big),\quad \overrightarrow{CK}=\Big(\tfrac{-13958}{1625},\tfrac{5544}{1625}\Big).$$
$$\overrightarrow{CH}\times\overrightarrow{CK}=\frac{-42\cdot5544\cdot4+99\cdot13958}{32500}=\frac{-931392+1381842}{32500}=\frac{450450}{32500},$$
$$\overrightarrow{CH}\cdot\overrightarrow{CK}=\frac{42\cdot13958\cdot4+99\cdot5544}{32500}=\frac{2344944+548856}{32500}=\frac{2893800}{32500}.$$
$$\tan\angle HCK=\frac{450450}{2893800}=\frac{33}{212}.\;\checkmark$$

Both angles equal $\theta$, confirming the stated condition, with

$$\boxed{\tan(\theta)=\dfrac{33}{212}}.$$

